Derived from src/devtmpfs/ (the PLZ110 6.12 port); same adaptations, plus:
- 6.1 VFS calls take &init_user_ns instead of &nop_mnt_idmap, and
  is_blockdev() is local as in the 6.1 source.
- Loading is gated like the GKI namespace payloads: gki=1 and a matching
  android14-6.1 release (or the build VM), with the userspace ABI check.
- kprobe mode (auto on Samsung EL2, or kprobe_hooks=1): device_add and
  device_del get entry kprobes that move the PC to the replacements; the
  native functions are reached through x16-marked stubs. No kernel or
  module text is written.

Samsung KDP kernels (CONFIG_KDP_CRED): build with scripts/build-samsung.py
against the vendor source and the device's own config. The worker's cred
handling (get_current_cred/override_creds) must use the vendor's KDP-aware
inlines; a GKI-header build writes the protected cred and the device resets
inside the start path. A GKI-header build now refuses to load when it finds
kdp_usecount_inc. Validated on SM-S921N (S5E9945, 6.1.162-android14-11,
firmware S921NKSUHEZIF) with vendor source 6.1.138: ready=1 errors=0 and
device nodes populated, alongside the kprobe-mode namespace module.
